Executive Summary:&nbsp;




The Kremlin has returned only a small share of the Ukrainian children it transferred to Russia since its full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Ukraine has documented more than 20,000 forced transfers of children, only 2,404 of which have been returned.&nbsp;



Forcibly separating children from their parents during filtration (фильтрация, fil’tratsiia)— Russia’s compulsory security screening of Ukrainian civilians in occupied territories—is one of six major mechanisms Russia has used to deport Ukrainian children to Russia, illustrating the coercive nature of separations and deportations.&nbsp;



Russia uses deported Ukrainian children to address Russia’s demographic decline and replenish its future military ranks. Nearly 47,000 Ukrainian children received Russian citizenship between April 2022 and June 2023.&nbsp;&nbsp;



